{"name":"Hippolyta","hex":"#cfc294","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Hippolyta","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An Amazonian queen who possessed a magic girdle given to her by her father, Ares.","A female given name from Ancient Greek."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Hippolyta"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hippolyta","blocks":[{"text":"In Greek mythology, Hippolyta, or Hippolyte, was the queen of the Amazons and a daughter of Ares and Otrera. Her sisters were Antiope and Melanippe. She wore her father Ares' zoster, which means 'war belt' or 'girdle' in Ancient Greek. Hippolyta figures prominently in the myths of both Heracles and Theseus. The name Hippolyta translates as \"she who unleashes the horses\", deriving from two Greek roots meaning \"horse\" and \"let loose\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Hippolyte_Amazon_queen.jpg/330px-Hippolyte_Amazon_queen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hippolyta","wikidata":"Q210303"},{"title":"Hippolyta (DC Comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Queen Hippolyta is a superhero appearing in American comic books published by DC Comics. She is the mother of Wonder Woman, and based on the Amazon queen Hippolyta from Greek mythology. Introduced in 1941 during the Golden Age of Comic Books, she is the queen of the Amazons of Themyscira, and in some continuities, the adopted mother of Donna Troy."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/90/Hippolyta_%28DC_Comics_character_circa_2022%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hippolyta_(DC_Comics)","wikidata":"Q3801710"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Nicolaes_Kn%C3%BCpfer_-_Hercules_Obtaining_the_Girdle_of_Hyppolita_-_WGA12217.jpg/500px-Nicolaes_Kn%C3%BCpfer_-_Hercules_Obtaining_the_Girdle_